    {
      "text": "So, let's set the rules properly, because the details decide everything. Every person on Earth gets a floating number, clearly visible, showing the balance in their primary account, real-time, updated by the second. It cannot be hidden, edited, or faked. It doesn't show your salary. It doesn't show your debt. It shows what you have right now. That's the whole rule. There's no second rule. And the first thing that happens, the very first thing, is that money stops being a number you know and starts being a number you're compared by. Because here's what we don't usually admit. We already publish almost everything else about our status. Your car is public. Your house is public. Your job title is public. Your clothes, your watch, your phone, the street you live on, all of it is a signal broadcast continuously for free. Money is the one thing that stayed hidden, and it stayed hidden because it is the only number that can't be faked. A car can be leased. Clothes can be copied. The number in your account cannot lie to anyone, which brings us to the first 24 hours.",
      "start_time": 0.24,
      "end_time": 65.68,
